# APT pinning preferences - https://wiki.debian.org/AptPreferences
#
# Copied in before the package lists are installed (live-build's
# includes.chroot_before_packages), so the image is built with the same
# kernel the installed system will track. From includes.chroot it only
# took effect at live-build's final upgrade, which then pulled a newer
# backports kernel's headers in at the last moment and DKMS failed there.

##### Kernel / firmware

Package: linux-image-*
Pin: release a=stable-backports
Pin-Priority: 600

Package: linux-headers-*
Pin: release a=stable-backports
Pin-Priority: 600

# Backports kernels pre-depend on a newer linux-base than stable has.
Package: linux-base
Pin: release a=stable-backports
Pin-Priority: 600

Package: firmware-*
Pin: release a=stable-backports
Pin-Priority: 600

##### NVIDIA proprietary drivers

Package: nvidia-driver
Pin: release a=stable-backports
Pin-Priority: 600

